# By its rows the iteration of a Map hands out entries. Where one pattern of two elements alone takes them, the step through the table makes no pair: key and value go on beside what the protocol hands out,
# and the pattern asks in its own place what the step asks: the Map: the two parts; anything else: the one operation that takes a pattern apart.
# function each(map: Map<string, number>) { for (const [key, value] of map) keep(key, value); }
